# What the `tests` job in .github/workflows/gates.yml asks for, before resolution.
#
# The job installs the COMPILED sibling, `ci-tests.txt`, which names this set plus everything it
# drags in, each with its hashes. This file is the intent; that one is what runs.
#
# Regenerate with, from the repository root:
#   pip-compile --generate-hashes --strip-extras --output-file=requirements/ci-tests.txt \
#       requirements/ci-tests.in
#
# A LINE IS ADDED HERE BY A DECISION, NEVER BY CONVENIENCE (D-30). This file used to end "NOTHING
# ELSE BELONGS HERE", on the ground that `tests/test_door_matches_ci.py` and
# `tests/test_reissue_obligation.py` hand-parse YAML because this job installs pytest and
# pytest-cov and nothing more. That ground is gone as of D-32 and the two docstrings resting on it
# are corrected in the same commit - a rule written in more than one place survives its own repeal
# (L-2), and the repealed copy here would have been the one that kept the other two sounding
# reasoned. What has NOT changed is the bar: the third line below is here because RED-031 proved
# that nothing in this repository loads a workflow the way GitHub does, and a fourth needs its own
# entry in DECISIONS.md, not a hurried edit.
pytest
pytest-cov
# D-32: `tests/test_workflows_parse.py` asks the real parser whether GitHub can read the files that
# run every gate. A hand-written scanner cannot answer that question - being more permissive than
# the machine it stands in for is the whole defect it would be written to catch.
pyyaml
